      "text": "Cancún, Chichén Itzá and a cenote"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "0adcc806b1bd872fc19c2a3328dd9736b5f90313b5a613d1aae6ee395a997c04",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-97d3eeec2bfb-mw9olsy5",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. Lunch is included.\n\nTravel to Chichén Itzá, about 120 km east of Mérida. One of the best-known and best-preserved Maya archaeological sites in the Yucatán, it is also one of the New Seven Wonders of the World. The ruins stand amid dense tropical vegetation.\n\nOn the tour, you’ll see the precisely laid out Pyramid of Kukulcán, the Great Ball Court, the largest in Mesoamerica, and the Sacred Cenote. This natural sinkhole was used for human sacrifices. The walk also takes in other temples in the complex.\n\nContinue to the cenote at Hacienda Selva Maya, where you can swim, have lunch and relax before returning to Cancún."
    },
